1
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:18,734
HPSEDC officers sign in with an administrator account.

2
00:00:18,794 --> 00:00:23,783
The Admin Console is the oversight and configuration centre for the portal.

3
00:00:23,843 --> 00:00:29,774
Along the top are one-click CSV exports of candidates, jobs, applications and placements.

4
00:00:29,834 --> 00:00:38,524
The left menu is grouped into overview and analytics, people, operations, risk and compliance, communication, and system settings.

5
00:00:38,584 --> 00:00:48,420
The overview shows registrations, open vacancies and placements, the application pipeline, candidates by district, and jobs by destination country.

6
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:02,870
Government vacancies usually arrive as an Excel or CSV file.

7
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:05,392
Open Import Jobs and choose the file.

8
00:01:05,452 --> 00:01:14,322
HireStream reads the columns and maps them automatically to job title, country, company, salary, number of vacancies and last date.

9
00:01:14,382 --> 00:01:16,231
You can correct any mapping.

10
00:01:16,291 --> 00:01:19,367
Every row is checked before anything is saved.

11
00:01:19,427 --> 00:01:27,479
Valid rows are green, warnings are amber, and rows with errors, such as a missing country, are red and will be skipped.

12
00:01:27,539 --> 00:01:31,705
Click Import to post the valid rows as live jobs under HPSEDC.

13
00:01:31,765 --> 00:01:34,160
Recent imports are listed for audit.

14
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:00,879
Professions controls the trades candidates choose from, and what each trade must hold.

15
00:02:00,939 --> 00:02:14,291
For each profession you can edit the English and Hindi names, the job categories it covers, the qualifications accepted, the specific skills list, the required and optional documents, and the note the candidate sees.

16
00:02:14,351 --> 00:02:17,831
Changes are live straight away, with no software release.

17
00:02:17,891 --> 00:02:20,066
Removing a profession only hides it.

18
00:02:20,126 --> 00:02:22,550
Candidates who already chose it keep it.

19
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:40,419
Form Fields lets HPSEDC decide what the application form asks.

20
00:02:40,479 --> 00:02:44,981
Each field can be shown or hidden, and marked must fill or optional.

21
00:02:45,041 --> 00:02:50,415
Fields with a padlock cannot be switched off, because the portal depends on them.

22
00:02:50,475 --> 00:02:52,764
A hidden field is never compulsory.

23
00:02:52,824 --> 00:02:58,265
Name, date of birth, gender, mobile, email and permanent address are always asked.

24
00:02:58,325 --> 00:03:06,920
Two entries are options rather than fields: the I do not have a passport yet choice, and the I am not sure option for ECR status.

25
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:18,263
System Config changes how the portal behaves, without a code release.

26
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:22,335
Every change is applied immediately and written to the audit log.

27
00:03:22,395 --> 00:03:31,107
The recruitment pipeline is set to Direct, four stages: applied, interview, selected and placed, with documents requested only at selection.

28
00:03:31,167 --> 00:03:35,743
Screened, six stages, can be switched on later if agencies are brought in.

29
00:03:35,803 --> 00:03:50,529
Other settings cover rejection rules, requiring a confirmed email before applying, the maximum number of trades per candidate, notification behaviour, file size limits, session security, and emigration compliance such as offer validity.

30
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:02,101
Users lists every account, with tabs for candidates, staff and all users.

31
00:04:02,161 --> 00:04:05,674
An administrator can disable or re-enable an account.

32
00:04:05,734 --> 00:04:10,932
Creating staff accounts and changing roles is done by the super administrator.

33
00:04:10,992 --> 00:04:14,842
Callbacks lists candidates who asked HPSEDC to phone them.

34
00:04:14,902 --> 00:04:17,067
Mark each one done after calling.

35
00:04:17,127 --> 00:04:23,270
Placement Support shows check-ins and problems reported by workers who are already overseas.

36
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:58,989
Compliance tracks the Emigration Act and MEA requirements across all candidates.

37
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:14,302
It shows passport, ECR, police clearance, medical, orientation and insurance coverage against targets, the visa pipeline, and risk flags, such as a worker placed without orientation or insurance, or a passport expiring within six months.

38
00:05:14,362 --> 00:05:19,794
Deployment Readiness shows who is travel ready and who is blocked, with a CSV export.

39
00:05:19,854 --> 00:05:27,290
Welfare SLA lists overdue thirty, sixty and ninety day welfare check-ins, so no worker is forgotten after departure.

40
00:05:52,760 --> 00:06:00,695
The Audit Log records every important action: status changes, setting changes and compliance updates, with who did it and when.

41
00:06:00,755 --> 00:06:03,276
You can filter it by resource and action.

42
00:06:03,336 --> 00:06:10,453
Fraud Watch collects reports from candidates who were asked for money, and highlights sudden spikes in grievances.

43
00:06:10,513 --> 00:06:17,630
Duplicates finds candidates who share an Aadhaar number, phone or email, so duplicate registrations can be merged.

44
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:54,168
Messages is the shared Ask HPSEDC inbox.

45
00:06:54,228 --> 00:06:59,021
Administrators can read and reply to candidates, as the placement team can.

46
00:06:59,081 --> 00:07:02,321
Grievances shows every complaint across the portal.

47
00:07:02,381 --> 00:07:09,439
Each moves from submitted, to under review, to action taken, and the complainant confirms when it is resolved.

48
00:07:09,499 --> 00:07:14,033
Notifications holds the message templates sent to candidates and staff.

49
00:07:14,093 --> 00:07:21,540
Each template's title and text can be edited, switched off, or set to hide the employer's name in negative messages.

50
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:26,894
Reports gives ready-made breakdowns by district, country, placement status, skill and sector, each downloadable as CSV.

51
00:08:26,954 --> 00:08:30,504
Funnel shows where candidates drop out between stages.

52
00:08:30,564 --> 00:08:38,458
Countries holds the destination information candidates read, such as visa rules, embassy contacts and labour law notes.

53
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:43,806
Lifecycle closes jobs past their deadline every night, and can be run on demand.

54
00:08:43,866 --> 00:08:49,020
Drives is where recruitment drives created by the placement team are approved.

